  "invariants": [
    "deterministic privacy/security/capability eligibility precedes learned routing and every cloud call",
    "LOCAL_ONLY never reaches OpenRouter or direct cloud",
    "task families are multi-label and workflows may be ordered multi-stage rather than a hybrid class",
    "routing engines are replaceable behind routing-mission and routing-decision contracts",
    "Hermes owns bounded workflow authority; a router framework cannot grant arbitrary tools or merge authority",
    "model roles are capability/economic pools and are not a one-to-one copy of task families",
    "OpenRouter normally chooses only the downstream physical provider for an already-selected eligible model",
    "OpenRouter Auto never becomes privacy, capability or final workflow authority",
    "required ZDR/tool/modality/context/network/sandbox facts cannot be weakened by a learned classifier or gateway fallback",
    "LCM and Mnemosyne are advisory context/memory, not execution authority",
    "orchestrator has no direct production coding authority after Pi cutover",
    "worker cannot self-merge",
